  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1130 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nAn upper-level trough over the Plains will push a surface cold \nfront through the area on Thursday, bringing little to no chance \nfor precipitation but some cooler temperatures to the area. \nAnother upper-level disturbance will enter the area on Saturday \nbringing a slight chance of scattered showers for the southern \nhalf of the area. Models then keep West Central Texas under drier \nconditions from Saturday night onward through the middle of next \nweek. High temperatures will generally remain in the 60s Friday \nand through much of the weekend, then gradually warm back into the\n70s for the first half of next week. Overnight lows are expected \nto remain in the mid 540s to lower 50s through the long term \nforecast.",
